---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import advocacyBg from "../../assets/photos/place-capitol-exterior.jpg";
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <Image
    src={advocacyBg}
    alt=""
    widths={[800, 1600, 2400]}
    sizes="100vw"
    data-parallax
    class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-[50%_35%] grayscale blur-[1px]"
  />
  <div
    class="absolute inset-0"
    style="background-color: rgba(250, 247, 238, 0.8);"
  ></div>

  <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="reveal font-display text-3xl font-normal text-navy-950">
      Advocacy
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="reveal card-lift rounded-xl border border-navy-950/15 bg-white p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-normal text-navy-950">
          SB 897: testifying at the California State Capitol
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-sage-700">
          California Senate and Assembly Education Committees · Sacramento, CA · 2024
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-navy-800">
          <p>
            In 2024, I testified before the California Senate and Assembly
            Education Committees on SB 897, the bill that made California's
            District of Choice program permanent, working alongside Senator
            Josh Newman and advocates from more than fifteen school districts
            statewide.
          </p>
          <p>
            District of Choice is the program that let me attend Walnut
            Valley schools instead of the district I would have been
            assigned to by default. I'd already lived what the bill was
            arguing for, so testifying for other students to have the same
            option felt like a tremendous honor and responsibility.
          </p>
          <p>
            The full hearing is archived through CalMatters' Digital
            Democracy project. My testimony starts around the 24:50 mark of
            the <a
              href="https://calmatters.digitaldemocracy.org/hearings/258116"
              class="font-semibold text-sage-700 underline decoration-sage-500 underline-offset-2 hover:text-sage-500"
              >official hearing record</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="reveal reveal-d2 card-lift rounded-xl border border-navy-950/15 bg-white p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-normal text-navy-950">
          Girl Scout Gold Award
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-navy-800">
          <p>
            For my Gold Award, I translated a court-mandated training manual
            into Spanish for the Latinx families it was supposed to serve,
            since the original English-only version was failing to fully
            support the community it was meant to reach.
          </p>
          <p>
            I also built mental health resource kits and educational
            materials for youth in foster care, and gave trauma-informed
            presentations to the school community.
          </p>
          <p>
            Girl Scouts later recognized me as a Lifetime Member.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="reveal reveal-d3 card-lift rounded-xl border border-navy-950/15 bg-white p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-normal text-navy-950">
          Bithiah's Family Services
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-navy-800">
          <p>
            My advocacy work started at Bithiah's Family Services when I was
            seven, volunteering at fundraisers, galas, and resource
            distribution events for foster and adoptive families. That's
            grown into a thirteen-year relationship, and since 2020 I've
            served as Coordinator of Volunteers, leading a bilingual
            initiative that has translated more than 80 pages of materials
            into Spanish and helped coordinate more than 50 supply
            distribution events. More detail on that role is on the <a
              href="/experience"
              class="font-semibold text-sage-700 underline decoration-sage-500 underline-offset-2 hover:text-sage-500"
              >Experience page</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
